# Working in this repository

Read `README.md` and `core/ENGINE.md` before changing anything. Everything in this repository is English.

## Three rules that outrank everything else

1. No client money. No costs, prices, day rates, budgets, tool spend or contract values of any client, in any file, template or test fixture
2. Nothing reaches the Notion board before the checks in `core/checks.md` pass
3. Markdown in `tenants/<tenant>/` is canonical configuration. Do not duplicate it elsewhere

## What Cursor does here

- Renderer and templates: `core/render/render.js`, the HTML templates, visual checks V1 to V7
- Reading and explaining the engine so the operator learns the code
- Small, reviewable edits with a Linear issue id (`COM-NN`) in the commit message

## What Cursor does not do here

- No writes to Notion, no runs of the engine. Runs happen in Claude Code (`/ce-run`, `/ce-render`, `/ce-learn`) because the connectors live there
- No new source types or clients in `tenants/` without an approved Linear issue
- No raw client material (transcripts, exports, emails) added to the repository

## Style

No em or en dashes in prose, periods or colons instead. No emojis. Bullets without trailing periods.
